WEBVTT

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:08.490
Your bento is ready!

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:15.740
Hey...

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:17.510
Did you hear me?

00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:22.150
Hey, your bento's-

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:24.560
Manabi?

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:28.670
Student Council President style!

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:35.880
Eh?

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:38.990
Look, turn around now

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:43.320
but things like chances won't be there anymore.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:47.780
That's what some people will tell you,

00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:54.030
but there are just times when you can't move at all.

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:03.510
Yes, everything I say

00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:07.950
is for your sake.

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:10.470
Sorry, but

00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:12.760
I won't consent easily

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:18.660
to things I don't accept.

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:25.640
Even if I can get by that moment with a lie

00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:28.720
I'll end up regretting it afterwards.

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:31.520
Whether it's the past or the future

00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:33.610
or, of course, the present,

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:38.020
I am the one that has to shoulder it.

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:42.700
You'll understand the meaning to everything afterwards.

00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:41.340
So let's worry!

00:01:42.730 --> 00:01:46.950
even if you don't understand them now,

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:51.620
whether it has to do with pain, fortune or secrets.

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:56.030
So don't cry, let's hold each other as we go

00:01:56.180 --> 00:01:59.510
forever-

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:05.270
It's My Life dakara

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:05.270
because it's my life.

00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:08.090
I'm off!

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:18.460
Seioh lower hill stop.

00:02:18.460 --> 00:02:19.760
Seioh lower hill stop.

00:02:20.210 --> 00:02:21.340
When boarding the bus-

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:22.310
Good morning.

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:24.130
Have you read this week's Love Melon?

00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:27.660
Next stop, Seioh High School.

00:02:24.130 --> 00:02:25.080
I did, I did.

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:27.670
There's an article featuring this summer's lovely animals.

00:02:27.670 --> 00:02:29.380
Ah, look over there.

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:36.970
Mei-chan! Good morning!

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:41.820
What is with her?!

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:43.480
The bus will be departing.

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:52.030
Good morning!

00:02:52.030 --> 00:02:53.090
M-Manabi-chan!

00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:53.910
Good morning!

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:56.100
G-Good morning.

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:57.210
It's morning~

00:02:58.060 --> 00:02:58.920
Yes.

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:00.860
And the weather's wonderful-

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:01.640
Indeed.

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:02.920
So...

00:03:03.630 --> 00:03:06.780
Forward go!! All day!!

00:03:12.010 --> 00:03:14.370
Eh, am I saying it, too?

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:23.970
Forward go. All day.

00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:32.490
Yo, good morning.

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:32.490
Good morning.

00:03:32.490 --> 00:03:34.240
Manabi-chan, don't cry!

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:35.440
Hey!

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:37.130
Hmm? What's going on?

00:03:37.130 --> 00:03:38.020
What's the matter?

00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:39.990
That didn't sound right...

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:11.730
This Miyasako Kenji's <i>Restaurant With a Small Menu  is one of the Kenji's representative works.</i>

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:14.760
Additionally, it was also a criticism of the zeitgeist of his era...

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:17.920
...and was a controversial aspect that was disputed in many ways.

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:20.830
According to the authority in ethnology, Yanagida Kunihiro,

00:04:20.830 --> 00:04:24.260
how the main character gets covered with various spices...

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:26.650
...and gets devoured in the end resembles Japan's rapid growth...

00:04:26.650 --> 00:04:29.210
...due to influence from
the US after the loss in the war.

00:04:33.590 --> 00:04:38.680
A week has passed since Manabi-chan took office.

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:42.400
Manabi-chan is always so full of energy,

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:46.610
in fact, so full of energy that she overwhelms me,

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:51.530
but for some reason,
I am also quite excited by her presence.

00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:58.520
What is it with those two?

00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:03.470
The Student Council President from
Aikoh High School is going to come visit Manabi,

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:05.410
so they're going to clean up the Student Council Office.

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:07.940
Aikoh's Student Council President?

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:10.190
We are sister schools, after all.

00:05:10.190 --> 00:05:12.340
It's probably a courtesy visit-

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:13.200
Mutsuki!

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:15.220
Ah, I'll be right there!

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:21.350
Are you going to be studying in the library today, too?

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:23.070
What's that got to do with you?

00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:29.100
How about paying them a visit on your way home?

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:30.830
I am not going!

00:05:32.210 --> 00:05:34.520
So, basically...

00:05:35.210 --> 00:05:36.180
Okay.

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:38.320
Let's begin our major cleanup.

00:05:39.970 --> 00:05:40.920
Yeah!

00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:42.240
Are you okay?

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:44.350
I am! Go on!

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:53.160
There are things to look out for during cleanup.

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:56.480
Items around here are placed in different areas, each based upon their own time period.

00:05:56.480 --> 00:05:57.660
On a picture...

00:05:58.490 --> 00:06:00.170
...it'd look like this.

00:06:03.660 --> 00:06:07.420
Depending on the areas' period,
some items could be very fragile, so...

00:06:13.750 --> 00:06:18.450
...please try not to touch things you think might be dangerous.

00:06:18.450 --> 00:06:20.600
U-Understood.

00:07:32.450 --> 00:07:33.870
See ya.

00:07:33.870 --> 00:07:34.860
Yeah!

00:07:36.970 --> 00:07:37.920
Now then...

00:07:43.430 --> 00:07:44.520
Yo!

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:45.780
How's the cleanup coming?

00:07:47.370 --> 00:07:49.100
Hey?

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:51.220
Eh?

00:07:53.170 --> 00:07:54.080
Hello?

00:07:54.940 --> 00:07:56.320
Hello?

00:07:59.550 --> 00:08:01.930
It's not that funny!

00:08:01.930 --> 00:08:03.150
Sorry, sorry.

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:06.960
To apologize, I'll help out, too.

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:08.520
Mu-chi!

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:09.810
Really?

00:08:10.270 --> 00:08:12.400
You can count on me!

00:08:17.550 --> 00:08:19.830
Ah, I just saw a comet.

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:24.030
Hope it's clear and sunny tomorrow.

00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:27.820
Same here.

00:08:42.370 --> 00:08:44.350
How about paying them a visit on your way home?

00:08:47.240 --> 00:08:48.940
I'll go buy some juice.

00:08:50.970 --> 00:08:52.120
What do you guys want?

00:08:56.470 --> 00:08:59.030
So you did come to take a look after all.

00:08:59.030 --> 00:09:02.310
I-I thought I'd cool down with the breeze on the roof before I go home.

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:05.030
Are you saying you'll help us?

00:09:05.030 --> 00:09:05.790
Huh?!

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:07.920
Well, well.

00:09:08.260 --> 00:09:09.410
W-Wait!

00:09:10.340 --> 00:09:11.650
Hey guys!

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:13.530
Mei's here to help out!

00:09:19.020 --> 00:09:22.590
To perform a nice cleanup, there needs to be order!

00:09:24.150 --> 00:09:25.710
Go, Sensei!

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:30.210
As such, we need to eliminate useless things.

00:09:30.210 --> 00:09:31.250
Delete them!

00:09:32.030 --> 00:09:32.510
Useless!

00:09:32.870 --> 00:09:33.430
Eliminate!

00:09:33.660 --> 00:09:34.550
Delete!

00:09:38.740 --> 00:09:41.410
Somehow when Mei says it, it sounds persuasive.

00:09:41.740 --> 00:09:43.520
You're just too sloppy.

00:09:46.570 --> 00:09:49.240
Anyhow, you throw away useless things.

00:09:49.240 --> 00:09:50.880
Only after that can everything else begin.

00:09:50.880 --> 00:09:52.120
That's it for today.

00:09:52.120 --> 00:09:53.990
Wow, it's so late already.

00:09:56.670 --> 00:09:57.720
Okay!

00:09:58.040 --> 00:10:00.270
We'll continue this tomorrow.

00:10:00.270 --> 00:10:02.790
Hey, how about we all go eat something together?

00:10:03.320 --> 00:10:04.710
I'm a gourmet, so ramen for me!

00:10:04.710 --> 00:10:05.960
I want McDonald's.

00:10:05.960 --> 00:10:08.180
Manabi, you're a ramen person, right?

00:10:09.760 --> 00:10:12.140
The ramen there is really delicious.

00:10:13.130 --> 00:10:15.230
McDonald's is good, too.

00:10:15.230 --> 00:10:16.630
No, definitely ramen.

00:10:23.580 --> 00:10:26.410
Mei-chan, which do you prefer, ramen or McDonald's?

00:10:30.840 --> 00:10:31.790
Umm...

00:10:35.740 --> 00:10:38.290
I-I have something to do!

00:10:50.520 --> 00:10:52.060
Mei-chan!

00:10:53.680 --> 00:10:56.240
Thanks for your advice!

00:11:00.530 --> 00:11:01.620
Let me make this clear!

00:11:01.620 --> 00:11:04.190
I really didn't go there meaning to help out!

00:11:14.660 --> 00:11:16.490
She's so not sincere.

00:11:19.450 --> 00:11:21.170
Eliminate all useless things...

00:11:21.170 --> 00:11:22.280
Delete, eh?

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:26.670
This Mei-chan is pretty mature.

00:11:26.670 --> 00:11:28.330
Right? Right?

00:11:28.330 --> 00:11:30.110
The complete opposite of you.

00:11:32.340 --> 00:11:35.570
I'm mature, too!

00:11:37.090 --> 00:11:39.970
There are things that children do which adults can't.

00:11:40.330 --> 00:11:42.380
Don't call me a child!

00:11:44.520 --> 00:11:45.620
A grain of rice.

00:11:46.510 --> 00:11:50.220
With grains of rice still sticking next to your mouth, you still have a long way to go.

00:11:53.100 --> 00:11:55.530
No!

00:11:55.530 --> 00:11:57.330
That place is for things we need.

00:11:57.330 --> 00:11:58.710
Things we don't need, put over there!

00:11:58.710 --> 00:11:59.870
Yeah, yeah.

00:12:00.090 --> 00:12:01.910
Are we done dividing the stuff?

00:12:01.910 --> 00:12:03.270
Y-Yeah.

00:12:03.270 --> 00:12:04.350
That's all.

00:12:05.410 --> 00:12:07.650
We took out all the useless things, right?

00:12:07.650 --> 00:12:09.120
All right!

00:12:09.120 --> 00:12:10.860
We're done.

00:12:10.860 --> 00:12:13.130
*clap* *clap* *clap* *clap*

00:12:13.130 --> 00:12:15.650
The elimination of useless things and deletion.

00:12:16.210 --> 00:12:17.050
By the way,

00:12:17.710 --> 00:12:18.760
what are those boxes?

00:12:29.940 --> 00:12:30.970
Scoop.

00:12:30.970 --> 00:12:33.840
The true form of the stray cat living on campus.

00:12:33.840 --> 00:12:35.810
That's not doable.

00:12:35.810 --> 00:12:37.240
Welcome, welcome!

00:12:38.780 --> 00:12:40.220
Welcome, welcome!

00:12:40.220 --> 00:12:41.370
Come, come.

00:12:41.370 --> 00:12:43.160
Come over and take a look!

00:12:43.160 --> 00:12:45.260
You don't need to pay if you're just taking a look.

00:12:45.260 --> 00:12:48.210
It's the Seioh Student Council
business-closing liquidation bazaar.

00:12:48.210 --> 00:12:51.250
W-We're not going out of business, Mu-chi!

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:53.600
Welcome, welcome!

00:12:52.850 --> 00:12:53.980
Geez...

00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:55.120
Welcome!

00:12:53.980 --> 00:12:55.600
To think we're doing something like this...

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:56.900
Ah, it's Momo-chan!

00:12:57.340 --> 00:13:00.090
What are you guys doing?

00:13:00.520 --> 00:13:02.580
A bazaar for useless things.

00:13:02.580 --> 00:13:04.700
You buy something, too, Momo-chan.

00:13:05.940 --> 00:13:07.740
That's a flower vase.

00:13:07.740 --> 00:13:10.820
I put a ribbon on a flask that was lying around.

00:13:13.310 --> 00:13:14.160
And this?

00:13:14.570 --> 00:13:16.890
Umm that's...

00:13:17.410 --> 00:13:19.120
...a cursed item.

00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:20.930
It's a wall adornment!

00:13:20.930 --> 00:13:22.280
How rude of you!

00:13:22.280 --> 00:13:24.530
Umm, how much is this?

00:13:24.950 --> 00:13:26.770
Everything's 50 yen.

00:13:26.820 --> 00:13:28.730
Really? Everything's 50 yen?

00:13:30.050 --> 00:13:31.230
Welcome!

00:13:33.470 --> 00:13:35.320
She said they're just 50 yen.

00:13:35.320 --> 00:13:36.760
Let's go take a look.

00:13:37.120 --> 00:13:37.760
Me, too.

00:13:40.760 --> 00:13:42.410
Oh no, we're out of change!

00:13:42.410 --> 00:13:43.640
What should we do?

00:13:43.640 --> 00:13:45.160
Gosh!

00:13:45.160 --> 00:13:47.160
You guys, line them up properly already!

00:13:47.160 --> 00:13:49.770
Tell them to give us 50 yen coins so that we don't have to deal with change!

00:13:54.980 --> 00:13:56.510
We have a problem here.

00:13:56.510 --> 00:14:00.150
I can't believe they're selling Student Council equipment for their own allowances.

00:14:00.150 --> 00:14:01.930
Go stop them, Principal.

00:14:05.250 --> 00:14:06.700
Sorry.

00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:08.430
Oh no, you got water all over the place!

00:14:08.430 --> 00:14:10.750
Gosh, the test papers are all...

00:14:11.210 --> 00:14:14.960
What are you doing, Shimojima-sensei?!

00:14:22.260 --> 00:14:23.450
Oh, well...

00:14:24.580 --> 00:14:27.450
Now, how is this going to turn out?

00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:34.380
Report.

00:14:34.380 --> 00:14:36.560
Our useless item bazaar resulted in...

00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:39.170
3250 yen in sales!

00:14:41.150 --> 00:14:42.160
Additionally,

00:14:42.160 --> 00:14:44.640
funds that were buried under all the items before were found...

00:14:44.640 --> 00:14:46.400
...for another 1230 yen.

00:14:48.280 --> 00:14:49.300
And finally,

00:14:49.610 --> 00:14:52.790
as a special boost, our adviser, Shimojima-sensei,

00:14:52.790 --> 00:14:55.800
has given us 5000 yen.

00:14:55.800 --> 00:14:57.550
So dazzling...

00:14:57.550 --> 00:14:59.670
Shimoji, you're rich!

00:15:04.200 --> 00:15:05.180
In conclusion,

00:15:05.430 --> 00:15:09.700
our special budget is now 9480 yen,

00:15:09.700 --> 00:15:13.880
and so, I thought we'd use this money
to change the image of this room a bit.

00:15:13.880 --> 00:15:15.260
Let's go eat something.

00:15:15.910 --> 00:15:18.720
Why don't we get some new curtains?

00:15:18.720 --> 00:15:20.460
And a new table and new chairs.

00:15:20.460 --> 00:15:21.950
Let's go eat something.

00:15:21.950 --> 00:15:24.030
Do you only think about food?

00:15:24.030 --> 00:15:27.850
Let's ask Shimojima-sensei to drive us after school to buy supplies!

00:15:27.850 --> 00:15:28.970
All right, we're going?

00:15:28.970 --> 00:15:30.450
We're not going to eat, okay?

00:15:30.450 --> 00:15:32.480
Eh? But I'm starving.

00:15:32.480 --> 00:15:33.090
Gosh.

00:15:33.090 --> 00:15:34.130
Wait!

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:36.620
What?

00:15:36.620 --> 00:15:39.120
We don't have enough money.

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:40.990
We'll just buy what we can.

00:15:40.990 --> 00:15:44.970
Besides, it's money we worked hard to make.

00:15:44.970 --> 00:15:47.280
Let's use it on something bigger!

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:50.230
Not on image changing...

00:15:50.230 --> 00:15:51.890
...But on something bigger?

00:15:53.740 --> 00:15:55.150
A remodeling!

00:15:57.880 --> 00:17:23.800
PLACEHOLDER

00:15:57.880 --> 00:16:08.770
Live the present moment, the season of encounters.

00:16:11.900 --> 00:16:22.860
The bright sunlight, the gathering of dreams.

00:16:23.880 --> 00:16:30.460
The miracle where people walk through the same youth.

00:16:30.950 --> 00:16:41.030
Cherry-blossom colored futures fly into the sky.

00:16:41.530 --> 00:16:55.150
Ah, the cheerful sounds of Seioh!

00:16:55.600 --> 00:17:09.880
Ah, let the beauty of learning at Seioh resonate!

00:17:10.170 --> 00:17:23.820
When we shine, we shine with our friends.

00:17:30.370 --> 00:17:32.950
Hey, sit down because it's dangerous.

00:17:33.190 --> 00:17:34.600
Okay.

00:17:39.060 --> 00:17:40.100
Forward, Go-

00:17:44.160 --> 00:17:47.450
Hey, that's why I said sit down.

00:17:53.630 --> 00:17:55.100
I beg of you!

00:17:55.470 --> 00:17:59.310
Why do we have to help out the Student Council?

00:17:59.310 --> 00:18:01.400
You know the saying: leave the work to the experts.

00:18:01.400 --> 00:18:03.640
So, please, help us build our interior.

00:18:03.970 --> 00:18:06.080
Our budget's been cut all these years,

00:18:06.080 --> 00:18:07.820
so we'll think about it if you increase it.

00:18:07.820 --> 00:18:09.400
Hey, we can't help that.

00:18:09.400 --> 00:18:11.280
With less and less students,

00:18:11.280 --> 00:18:13.830
even sports clubs have it tough with budgets.

00:18:14.130 --> 00:18:16.690
Then, go ask the sports club people.

00:18:16.690 --> 00:18:19.250
We don't get to be here other than lunch time,

00:18:19.250 --> 00:18:21.970
so we don't want to waste time on something like this.

00:18:22.290 --> 00:18:23.680
What?!

00:18:24.480 --> 00:18:25.340
Chairman, Chairman.

00:18:25.340 --> 00:18:26.030
What?!

00:18:26.580 --> 00:18:28.010
U-Umm, look at this.

00:18:28.340 --> 00:18:33.010
In preparations for tomorrow's courtesy visit from Aikoh High School's Student Council President,

00:18:33.010 --> 00:18:35.720
we're bringing you a live broadcast from our Student Council office.

00:18:36.880 --> 00:18:41.730
Well then, how has the Student Council office been remodeled?

00:18:41.960 --> 00:18:45.040
Let us take a look inside.

00:18:45.470 --> 00:18:48.170
Hey, you help out, too!

00:18:48.680 --> 00:18:52.160
I'm not a Student Council officer.

00:18:52.160 --> 00:18:53.760
Neither am I!

00:18:54.490 --> 00:18:57.140
So, why are you helping out?

00:18:57.140 --> 00:18:59.750
W-Why does that matter?

00:19:00.580 --> 00:19:01.920
The design theme is a cafe.

00:19:03.690 --> 00:19:09.450
Well then, let us interview Student Council President Amamiya Manami for the concept behind this design.

00:19:11.970 --> 00:19:12.890
Me?

00:19:13.130 --> 00:19:15.840
Why change the office into a cafe?

00:19:17.210 --> 00:19:18.500
Umm...

00:19:32.210 --> 00:19:33.150
A place to hang out.

00:19:33.510 --> 00:19:35.660
I wanted to build a hangout.

00:19:35.930 --> 00:19:38.110
A hangout?

00:19:38.810 --> 00:19:39.680
Yes.

00:19:39.680 --> 00:19:40.990
Umm...

00:19:40.990 --> 00:19:45.560
I thought I should start by creating a place where everyone can gather and enjoy their time.

00:19:45.560 --> 00:19:49.760
So I thought we should make it
a cute, nice-looking place.

00:19:50.370 --> 00:19:53.760
So, this is a place for the entire school to hang out.

00:19:54.540 --> 00:19:59.670
This is a cafe where we welcome anyone that loves this school.

00:19:59.670 --> 00:20:02.390
It doesn't matter if you're not a Student Council officer.

00:20:03.290 --> 00:20:05.500
Whether you're from a sports club or a social club,

00:20:05.500 --> 00:20:08.420
people that go straight home, people that need something, people that have nothing to do,

00:20:08.420 --> 00:20:10.650
please come here whenever you want!

00:20:10.900 --> 00:20:14.130
We'll be waiting for you with drinks and delicious snacks.

00:20:14.130 --> 00:20:16.620
Let's chat about things around the school together!

00:20:17.190 --> 00:20:22.320
And let's make every day of our school life bright and exciting!

00:20:22.320 --> 00:20:25.580
And then the school will become much more fun, so...

00:20:27.710 --> 00:20:30.870
Forward, go!

00:20:31.610 --> 00:20:36.190
And those were
President Amamiya Manami's comments.

00:20:42.140 --> 00:20:44.270
A job well done, Manabi-chan.

00:20:45.400 --> 00:20:47.060
I'm kind of tired now.

00:20:47.960 --> 00:20:50.280
Well, you worked hard.

00:20:51.090 --> 00:20:52.270
Umm...

00:20:53.030 --> 00:20:54.580
We're from the gardening club.

00:20:55.500 --> 00:20:57.910
If you'd like, please use these flowers.

00:21:01.890 --> 00:21:03.530
Thank you!

00:21:07.470 --> 00:21:08.830
If you want to make some curtains,

00:21:08.830 --> 00:21:10.550
the handcraft club can help out.

00:21:10.550 --> 00:21:12.550
If you're going to move heavy things, let us know.

00:21:12.550 --> 00:21:14.360
My family runs an electronics store, so-

00:21:18.330 --> 00:21:19.410
OW!

00:21:19.410 --> 00:21:21.240
I can't watch this.

00:21:25.130 --> 00:21:27.580
And? What do we need to do?

00:21:27.580 --> 00:21:29.260
Tables? Chairs?

00:21:29.880 --> 00:21:32.170
Whether we're from a sports club or a social club, eh?

00:21:32.720 --> 00:21:36.370
Putting it that way would make me look like a bad guy, right?

00:21:37.260 --> 00:21:38.440
We're in your debt.

00:21:40.210 --> 00:21:41.170
Okay!

00:21:41.550 --> 00:21:42.830
Let's do it!

00:21:43.800 --> 00:21:45.390
Forward...

00:21:45.390 --> 00:21:46.880
GO!!!

00:23:22.560 --> 00:23:23.920
Excuse me.

00:23:30.060 --> 00:23:32.290
Aikoh High School Student Council President-
